WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.610
In 2167...

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.760
...the Earth suffered incredible damage...

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.990
...from the supernova of the star.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.640
But people all over the world have united together to survive.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.360
People of the past, thank you so much.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.670
The Earth is well.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.740
And I'm doing good as well somehow.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.360
It's the year 2356.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:05.020
Episode Seven:
Frustration

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:14.590
Good morning, fellows!

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.100
Oh! The star of hope!

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:19.980
You're incredible, Shipon.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.530
They say that you ranked twelfth on this past test.

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.930
When I saw the bulletin board, I was doubtful...

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.180
...since just until recently, it felt like you were baggage.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.320
So well done, well done.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.030
It might be that you're the only one that's baggage now.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.130
Leave me alone!

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.590
But it really is an incredible rise.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.420
Yeah. Your increase in skill isn't half-rate.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.290
But, but, Yayoi is so much, so much higher than me!

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.690
With your current drive...

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.980
...your  passing me might just be a question of time.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:52.140
What...?

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.510
I-I wonder...

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.010
You're already thinking about it, too...

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:56.970
Eh!

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.340
Well, more than anything else, it's just that, you know...

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.680
You're amazing!

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:03.700
Thank you...

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.280
Actually, I'm really happy!

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.020
Well, in that case...

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:13.300
In celebration of Shima Katase being in twelfth place...

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.140
...this meal will be on Shipon...

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.220
Thanks for the food!

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:18.540
What?

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.340
I'll take the usual!

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:23.890
What!?

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:25.510
Yes, me too.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.270
Thanks for treating.
 What!?

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:28.370
What!?

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.070
Thanks a lot!

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.800
Oh, why does it always end up like this?

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.340
Good morning.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:38.870
Oh...

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:40.400
Good morning!

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.340
A morning A, please.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:48.320
Um, two morning A's, and two B's, please.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.920
Hmm? What?

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.940
Huh, err, um...

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.010
You don't look at the bulletin board, do you?

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.470
Nope. Is there a class cancellation or something?

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.400
No, that's not it.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.390
You see, on the recent practical skill test...

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.060
Huh?

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.170
I got twelfth place...

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.770
Oh, incredible! You did it!

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:16.690
Thank you.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.800
You did very well. 

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.800
 Jinrai

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.770
Not bad. Keep doing your best, just like that.

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:09.660
Yes.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:16.630
Did you see them?

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.670
The results for the preparatory student's practical tests.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.950
There are a lot of things you're interested in, aren't there?

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.960
Curiosity is the source of knowledge.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.430
The girl who was at the very bottom is now an honor student.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.960
At first, she was terrible, so now she's all the more prominent.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.380
She's quite something.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:41.760
She might be a genius.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:43.900
What do you want to say, I wonder.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:45.950
No, nothing.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:51.800
Oh, amazing! She's truly a threat, a rival has appeared, what will I do!?

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.730
How was that reaction?

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:54.310
Oh...

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:57.550
So then, you don't think anything of her...

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:00.090
If I'm still concerned about the preparatory students...

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.210
...then I'm in no condition to be part of the Great Mission.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:02.990
Hm.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.890
Sorry to disturb your lunch.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:07.670
See you.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:26.500
Hey...

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.250
I wonder what our new training is going to be.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:32.080
Miss Leila's faint laughter from earlier has been bothering me so much...

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.700
...I can't help myself.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.890
It's probably the Lightning Joust.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:39.020
We're moving into pretty high level training.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:39.830
Hmm...

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:47.460
Huh?

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.190
What are you doing?

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:50.800
Examining my own mistakes.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:53.130
I'm analyzing today's data logger.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:54.230
Examining your own mistakes?

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.220
But you were completely perfect today.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:57.640
That's not true.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:01.720
Now that I've looked at this, it feels like I can still push the flight program.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:03.880
Just what I'd expect from someone in twelfth place!

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:05.160
I've lost sight of you!

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:06.140
Uh...

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:11.590
N-not my ribs!

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:14.240
Hmm... Weak spot found!

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:22.220
Hey.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.030
Hmm?

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:24.770
Do you enjoy studying?

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:26.640
Yes, very much.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:31.900
Now then, what should we do for dinner?

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:33.520
Up to you.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:37.020
Shipon, if you were a man, you'd definitely be the worst husband.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:07.210
Today's training is the Lightning Joust.

00:08:07.390 --> 00:08:09.110
The competition takes place on a field...

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:12.790
...that is 1.2 kilometers long by 0.4 kilometers wide and tall.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:14.590
The rules are simple.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:16.050
Using your own graviton generator...

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:18.610
...break your opponent's graviton balance...

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:19.820
...and knock them into the barrier.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:21.180
That's all.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:22.600
But!

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:25.050
Taking action that looks like you're going to slam into, contact...

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.410
...or directly approach your opponent will immediately disqualify you.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:27.800
Keep that in mind.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:31.680
Once you've entered the course you have five seconds until you cross.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.640
This is a competition where you put everything on the line...

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:36.300
...in the instant you pass each other.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:38.210
That is all! Any questions?

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.140
All right! Let's give it a try!

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:11.640
So slow...

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:14.530
They're scared, aren't they?

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:32.170
Huh...

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:35.030
Next!

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.680
Got you!

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:50.910
Kouta's so cool!

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:54.090
Pierre's so un-cool!
 Pierre's so un-cool!

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.850
Don't you guys say that!

00:09:58.770 --> 00:09:59.920
Next! Katase!

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.620
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:01.750
Fujisawa!

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:02.500
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.630
Huh! Um...

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:42.260
Oh, how frustrating...

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:46.140
Could it be that you missed the point of the training, Milady?

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:46.540
Eh?

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:47.870
No way.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:49.720
No, I might have...

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:53.160
Shipon, you really are incredible.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:54.480
Fujisawa!

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:59.870
Those movements weren't like you...

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:03.020
The difference between you and Katase isn't great enough...

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:04.150
...for you to be taken out so easily.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.330
Are you still... concerned about what happened then?

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:08.260
Tomorrow.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:12.110
Please watch during tomorrow's combined training.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:15.550
What I did yesterday will make me greater today...

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:19.160
...and what I do today will make me greater tomorrow.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.980
I came back here once I started thinking that way.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.990
The most important thing is that I want to improve myself.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.950
That's why I want you to please watch tomorrow.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:33.360
I see...

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:39.980
But, man, how I'll ever be able to control it like you, Shipon...

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:41.460
...is a mystery.

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:43.860
There you go again. You're over exaggerating.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:47.430
Really? The stunts that you do aren't something just anyone can do.

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:49.150
Aim for the universe!

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:53.460
Shima Katase! You are my star of hope!

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:58.230
But I'm your star? Then you're not going to aim for it, Arisa?

00:11:58.460 --> 00:11:59.240
Me?

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:01.670
Um... I'm going to pass on it.

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:02.250
What?

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:05.510
All of the people who come here are amazing.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.680
Even still, there are people who have good grades...

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:08.980
...and people who have bad grades.

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:11.100
I have bad ones...

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:14.860
That's not true! You're trying too, Arisa!

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.340
But my grades are only so-so.

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.590
My yearning to go into the universe won't change.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:24.280
How I feel won't lose out to anyone...

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:29.660
It's just, what would be the best choice for me...

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.350
I don't know what that is...

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:35.330
Arisa...

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:37.030
That's why I have to try even harder!

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:37.620
Huh?!

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:39.980
Do my best at our classes and our training...

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:43.080
...and quickly find the best path for me!

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:45.880
Then you're not quitting the school, right?

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:46.370
Huh?

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:49.530
I mean, it kind of felt like that...

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.750
What? Really?

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.210
Yeah... but, thank goodness...

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:00.480
Thank goodness... thank goodness...

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:03.460
Shipon...

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:07.350
Raising you to number one best friend status...

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:09.300
...really was the right thing to do, Shipon.

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:12.780
It's because you're like this, Shipon, that I cheer for you!

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.340
That I want to cheer for you!

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.760
So do your best, star of hope!

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:19.800
And stop crying.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.500
Thank you... Shipon.

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:35.070
That was quite a deep sigh.

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:37.820
Oh, good afternoon.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:38.890
Ah.

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:40.970
...or is it good evening?

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.860
I see, this is a tricky time of day.

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.910
So, are you worrying about love?

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:53.780
What?

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:59.230
Oh... somehow, I don't like that "whoosh" and "thud".

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:00.430
"Whoosh"?

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.020
And the "thud"...

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:12.000
Whoosh-thud, huh?

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.560
Do you have any thoughts on the combined training?

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:22.170
Hit them and break through!

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:23.750
So you're going to break through.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:26.850
Right, after all, our opponents are the regular students.

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:30.730
It feels like we won't know what will work, so we'll just have to try, I guess.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:34.150
That's true. But it's impolite to go empty-handed.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:35.970
Since we're practicing with more experienced people...

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:38.050
...we want to be as prepared as possible.

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:39.030
That's true.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:40.670
Our opponents are in Katie's.

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:43.950
The difference in ability between them and the normal Biancas is evident.

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:45.110
Optional parts?

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:47.970
Right. The Bianca's maneuverability can be a weapon.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:52.010
If you strengthen the thrusters, even if it isn't an even match...

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:54.650
...you might be able to catch them off guard, I think.

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:57.250
I see, I'll use that.

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:00.140
But...

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:03.550
...it might be better to concentrate on your settings.

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:04.190
What?

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:07.690
Well, your flying style is really pretty, Yayoi, so...

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.830
Hmm... What do you call it?

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:11.330
Refined?

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.890
Rather than improving your maneuverability through power...

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:19.200
...make the unit more like this, closer to yourself.

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:21.770
That kind of feeling? Just kidding!

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:24.890
That! That's good!

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:25.510
Huh?

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:28.490
You mean increasing the responsiveness of the controls...

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:30.500
...of one part of the unit... right?

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:31.370
That's it, right?

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:34.380
No matter how hard you try, your basic ability won't change.

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:37.680
In that case, creating a setting that matches your current self...

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:39.500
...it might be good...

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:42.330
That's great! Thank you!

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:43.930
W-well...

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:45.800
Hmmmmmm!

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:49.530
I'm not really sure, but the tension is rising!

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:52.800
We want to give the regular students a surprise, right?

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:54.770
Yeah! Let's do our best!

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:56.620
Y-yeah...
 Y-yeah...

00:15:57.510 --> 00:16:00.090
What's with that, you're not energetic at all...

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:02.370
It's around the time for them to start getting full of themselves, is it...?

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:01.940
Now, one more time! 

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:03.930
Here we go, one, two...

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:05.420
Let's do our best!

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:06.850
Yeah!

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:13.970
Today we're having combined training with the regular students!

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:16.600
Go and experience the difference in your levels!

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:17.670
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:29.290
Wh-what?

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:31.950
This is impossible!

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:34.080
They're being beaten too easily.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.530
Next! Fujisawa!

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:40.520
Yes, ma'am!

